/-!
# A finite generically étale map from an open enlargement of an affine curve

Source: Weil conjectures blueprint, `sec-deligne-laumon-a1/sk-thm-dl-a1-upper`,
`lem-a1-finite-map-curve.md` (blueprint: lem-a1-finite-map-curve).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits WeilConjectures

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- A smooth affine curve over the global finite field, geometrically a connected curve,
has a smooth geometrically connected open enlargement with finite complement and a finite
morphism to the affine line which is étale on a dense open of its source.
Source: Weil conjectures blueprint, `lem-a1-finite-map-curve.md`
(blueprint: lem-a1-finite-map-curve).

Proof:
1. Smoothness gives normality (lem-sc-smooth-normal). Finite type over the finite field
   gives Noetherianness and finitely many components
   (lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-over-noetherian, lem-weil-pbc-noetherian-finite-components).
   The smooth geometrically connected curve is geometrically integral. Take its smooth
   projective completion using lem-wf-curve-normal-smooth-compactification.
2. Its boundary is a finite nonempty set: otherwise the affine curve is proper, hence
   finite over the field by lem-sc-proper-affine-finite-general, contradicting dimension one.
   Choose a boundary closed point s, with finite separable residue degree d > 0.
3. The point is Cartier (lem-sc-point-cartier). Its inverse ideal powers O(ns) sit inside
   the function field (def-sc-function-field). Choose m prime to p with
   (m - 1)d > 2g - 2. Riemann--Roch (sk-thm-picard-rr) gives a dimension jump d between
   the sections of O(ms) and O((m - 1)s).
4. A section f in the difference has its sole pole at s, of exact order m. The sections
   1,f generate O(ms); lem-weil-pbc-sections-morphism-to-proj-polynomial-ring constructs
   h to the projective line with inverse image of infinity exactly {s}.
5. The projective line is proper (lemma-nagata-projective-space-base-change-proper).
   The map h is proper by lem-weil-pbc-proper-over-separated. It is nonconstant, so its
   closed fibres have dimension zero and are finite by lem-sc-dim0-finite; the generic
   fibre contains at most the generic point. The locally Noetherian target permits
   thm-pqf-finite-iff-proper-finite-fibres, giving finiteness of h.
6. By lem-a1-uniformizer-differential-basis, at s the local ring has uniformizer t with
   differentials freely generated by dt. Writing 1/f = t^m v, with v a unit and dv = a dt,
   gives d(1/f) = t^(m-1)(m v + t a) dt, which is nonzero since p does not divide m.
7. Apply lem-a1-nonzero-differential-generically-etale to obtain a nonempty open on which
   h is étale. Smoothness of the projective line is checked on its polynomial charts
   (def-sbc-smooth-morphisms).
8. Remove s from the completion. The resulting curve is the inverse image of the affine
   chart, so the restriction g is finite by lem-weil-pbc-finite-morphism-permanence.
   Its étale open remains dense. Smoothness and étaleness restrict to opens
   (def-sbc-smooth-morphisms, def-weil-etale-morphism). Its geometric base change is an
   open of the integral completion, hence a connected curve. It contains the original
   curve densely with finite complement, namely the remaining boundary points. -/
theorem exists_finite_genericallyEtale_curve_enlargement
    (D : FiniteFieldDatum.{u}) (C₀ : Over (Spec (.of D.k₀)))
    [IsCurve C₀.hom] [Smooth C₀.hom] [IsAffine C₀.left]
    [IsConnectedCurve (D.geometricFiber C₀).hom] :
    ∃ (C₀' : Over (Spec (.of D.k₀))) (hC₀' : IsCurve C₀'.hom),
      Smooth C₀'.hom ∧
      IsConnectedCurve
        (@FiniteFieldDatum.geometricFiber D C₀'
          hC₀'.toLocallyOfFiniteType hC₀'.toQuasiCompact).hom ∧
      ∃ (j : C₀ ⟶ C₀') (g : C₀'.left ⟶ 𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Spec (.of D.k₀))),
        IsOpenImmersion j.left ∧ DenseRange j.left ∧
        (Set.range j.left)ᶜ.Finite ∧
        g ≫ (𝔸(ULift.{u} (Fin 1); Spec (.of D.k₀)) ↘ Spec (.of D.k₀)) = C₀'.hom ∧
        IsFinite g ∧
        ∃ U : C₀'.left.Opens, Dense (U : Set C₀'.left) ∧ Etale (U.ι ≫ g) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
